{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>in the wilderness of Sinai</b> Above it is written אלה המצות, and adjacent to it 'in the wilderness' — to teach: if a person does not make himself like a wilderness, he cannot know Torah and commandments. Above it is written וכל מעשר בקר וצאן, and adjacent to it 'Take a count of' — as stated: עוד תעבורנה הצאן, by means of counting."], :book :numbers, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {0 "The final phrase עוד תעבורנה הצאן ע\"י מונה is rendered hyper-literally; the syntactic linkage between the verse quotation and 'by means of counting' is terse and possibly elliptical in the source."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:21:01.979710278Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}